WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.428
Where is leadership forming, and how many companies move with it?

00:00:04.428 --> 00:00:08.856
The Diffusion looks beneath IHSG. Follow a sector reading back to

00:00:08.856 --> 00:00:10.869
its companies, dates, and calculations.

00:00:11.229 --> 00:00:16.584
The Dashboard tracks 132 stocks across 11 IDX sectors, 12 per

00:00:16.584 --> 00:00:17.334
sector

00:00:17.334 --> 00:00:21.715
by market capitalization on 2 October 2026. This retrospective

00:00:21.715 --> 00:00:22.465
set

00:00:22.465 --> 00:00:25.386
does not cover every listed company.

00:00:25.219 --> 00:00:29.791
The main map places 60-day excess return against IHSG on the

00:00:29.791 --> 00:00:33.946
horizontal axis. The vertical axis is 20-day excess minus 60-day

00:00:33.946 --> 00:00:37.271
excess. Together, those coordinates show where a sector

00:00:37.271 --> 00:00:38.102
stands and

00:00:38.102 --> 00:00:41.842
how its momentum is changing. Leadership uses a separate

00:00:41.842 --> 00:00:45.166
calculation: 20-day excess and 5-day versus 60-day acceleration.

00:00:45.166 --> 00:00:45.916
A

00:00:45.916 --> 00:00:49.657
sector needs at least five eligible contributors before that

00:00:49.657 --> 00:00:50.407
signal

00:00:50.407 --> 00:00:51.238
is confirmed.

00:00:50.929 --> 00:00:55.441
Use the replay controls to move through 21 daily dates or five

00:00:55.441 --> 00:00:59.201
weekly dates, from 4 September through 2 October. The underlying

00:00:59.201 --> 00:01:02.962
price history starts on 9 June, providing the observations needed

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:04.842
for the displayed return windows.

00:01:05.202 --> 00:01:09.889
Select a sector to inspect its 20-day and 60-day excess returns,

00:01:09.889 --> 00:01:12.872
rotation phase, participation, and concentration. The equal-weight

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:17.133
basket uses the names available for each horizon and compares

00:01:17.133 --> 00:01:17.883
their

00:01:17.883 --> 00:01:20.865
prices with IHSG over the same dates.

00:01:20.901 --> 00:01:24.588
Coverage varies by stock and horizon. Dividends, splits, rights

00:01:24.588 --> 00:01:27.865
issues, and other mechanical events remove the affected

00:01:27.865 --> 00:01:28.615
windows.

00:01:28.615 --> 00:01:33.121
When an observation is missing, the calculation leaves it out; no

00:01:33.121 --> 00:01:36.397
missing price is filled. Contributor counts stay beside

00:01:36.397 --> 00:01:37.147
each

00:01:37.147 --> 00:01:37.897
reading.

00:01:37.236 --> 00:01:41.177
For breadth, the dashboard compares the same names at both

00:01:41.177 --> 00:01:41.927
dates.

00:01:41.927 --> 00:01:45.474
That paired count matters: a percentage can move as

00:01:45.474 --> 00:01:46.224
participation

00:01:46.224 --> 00:01:49.376
changes, while the displayed denominator shows how many

00:01:49.376 --> 00:01:50.126
companies

00:01:50.126 --> 00:01:51.309
were actually comparable.

00:01:50.601 --> 00:01:55.099
Coverage and Sources lists all 132 stocks, their latest closes, and

00:01:55.099 --> 00:01:59.188
the dates covered by their price histories. Those prices support

00:01:59.188 --> 00:01:59.938
the

00:01:59.938 --> 00:02:02.801
daily and weekly replay. Year-to-date readings and

00:02:02.801 --> 00:02:03.551
company-level

00:02:03.551 --> 00:02:08.458
flow remain tied to the original 66-stock set: 23 names have an

00:02:08.458 --> 00:02:13.365
action-free return, and company flow spans 5 July to 2 October. No

00:02:13.365 --> 00:02:15.819
sector reaches the five-name year-to-date threshold.

00:02:15.497 --> 00:02:20.154
The other pages combine distinct sources. Market Movers uses the

00:02:20.154 --> 00:02:23.415
official IDX Stock Summary. Market-level foreign-flow totals

00:02:23.415 --> 00:02:24.165
come

00:02:24.165 --> 00:02:27.891
from IDX Daily Statistics, alongside company flow from

00:02:27.891 --> 00:02:28.822
Sectors API.

00:02:28.822 --> 00:02:32.548
Broader adjusted-price comparisons use Yahoo Finance data through

00:02:32.548 --> 00:02:37.205
the yfinance Python client. Ownership uses dated IDX and KSEI

00:02:37.205 --> 00:02:40.931
disclosures; affiliation alone does not prove legal control.

00:02:41.007 --> 00:02:44.093
Methodology lays out the formulas, sources, thresholds, and

00:02:44.093 --> 00:02:47.950
exclusions. Use it to understand what each reading can support,

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:48.700
then

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:53.328
follow a sector back to its constituents. That is the point: a

00:02:53.328 --> 00:02:56.027
clearer view of leadership beneath the index.
